nodecode-fleetkeep is a rewrite of jlucwright's jlucwright/fleetkeep-agent-plugin:

  https://github.com/jlucwright/fleetkeep-agent-plugin
  commit 67c7334d21895cf38586d110d3dcc3c4e6cedeb9
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Studea Limited (LICENSE)

The original was one Agent Plugins v1 package with a single skill,
skills/fleetkeep-import-review/SKILL.md: prose that told a model to map a
vehicle spreadsheet onto Fleetkeep's six import columns, keep unknown dates
blank, flag ambiguous dates, duplicates, missing registrations and cells a
spreadsheet might run. Its rules, in the same order and with the same
cautions, are fleetkeep.lisp here: the same six columns, the same refusal to
guess a date that reads both ways, the same "keep the row and flag it" for a
registration, the same formula guard, the same "a column the six do not take
is named, not pretended in". The skill's prose is kept as (help :fleetkeep),
which is where the parts no arithmetic decides still live.

What the rewrite adds is the arithmetic: a CSV reader and writer that follow
RFC 4180, a review that answers with counts and one line per row, a tool the
model calls with the CSV text, and /fleetkeep for a file named at a shell.
What it left out is the original's packaging: the Agent Plugins manifest and
the duplicated .plugin/plugin.json a directory indexer read, its product
links and its README, which the cell's own README replaces. Nothing of the
original is bundled here, and nothing of it runs: the review is Lisp over
the text it is handed, with no key, no network and no account.
